  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward drift bias (approx +2.5 EUR) when recent history shows volatility but no sustained trend; subtract this fixed offset from forecasts.",
    "When sentiment spikes to 1.0 or -1.0, the model fails to capture immediate mean reversion and instead projects continued linear movement; apply a dampening factor of 0.6 to forecasted gains/losses following high-sentiment days.",
    "Model consistently underestimates volatility clusters (e.g., Example 5 where true outcome swung from 70.82 to 66.49); increase forecast variance by 15% during periods of mixed sentiment history.",
    "In volatile regimes, the model's 30-day horizon is too smooth; correct by introducing a 'noise floor' equal to the standard deviation of the last 5 days of actual price action.",
    "When recent history contains a sharp drop followed by recovery (e.g., Example 1), the model over-smooths the trough and should be adjusted downward by 3-4 EUR relative to its linear projection."
  ]
}
